EDAT reader: compressed-file support (flag 0x01): block layer plus the block decompressor. Before: any file with
EDAT_COMPRESSED_FLAG was refused outright (the old message also wrongly blamed "zlib"). Now the per-block table of a
compressed file (0x20-byte entries at 0x100) is decoded: for NPD version >= 2 each entry is 0x10 bytes of block hash
followed by 0x10 bytes (offset be64, stored length be32, "block is compressed" flag be32) masked with bytes of the
entry itself. Each block is located, hash-checked (CMAC/HMAC over the padded stored bytes, key as for plain blocks),
CBC-decrypted and, if its flag is set, decoded by edat_lz_decode() (adaptive binary range coder + LZ77 with
context-modelled literals; implemented from a written specification, own code, MIT); flag 0 blocks are copied.
Each block must decode to exactly block size (last block: file_size % block_size). Header byte > 0x80 means a raw
stored stream, header byte >= 11 means literal context 0, input overrun and range 0 are treated as corrupt data.
Debug-data flag (0x80000000) is still refused. Plain files: path unchanged. Applies after 5002.
Test: host program calling edat_decrypt_file on compressed SDATs of the disc (SCELOGO.BPM.sdat, 83040 bytes, etc.;
results in the RE notes). Upstream candidate.

